  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dehumanizing_metaphor",
  "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
  "instance_name": "dehumanizing_metaphor",
  "label": "Dehumanizing Metaphor",
  "description": "This refers to the use of metaphors or analogies that strip a person of their humanity, often by comparing them to inanimate objects or animals. In this case, comparing a person to a 'firecracker' reduces them to a volatile, explosive object, which can be seen as dehumanizing. This type of metaphor is often used to justify negative judgments or actions against the person, as it implies they are not worthy of empathy or understanding.",
